# Never upload local environment files to a build.
#
# `vercel deploy` from a terminal uploads the working tree and a `.gitignore` entry does not stop it. Without this, a developer's `.env` — real secrets, and `API_URL="http://localhost:3001"` — is shipped into the build container, 
# where Next.js loads it and inlines localhost into the browser bundle. The deploy succeeds, the pages render and every request from the browser goes to the reader's own machine.
#
# Vercel's own environment variables are the only source of configuration for a deployment. See docs/environment.md.
.env
.env.*

# Build output and caches — regenerated in the build container. `.vercel/output` especially: uploading a local Build Output API directory invites the build to pick up whatever was last built on somebody's laptop.
node_modules
.next
.turbo
.output
.eve
dist
.vercel/output

# Nothing here affects the build.
docs/images
adrs
